QUICKJS

  QuickJS is a small and embeddable Javascript engine by Fabrice Bellard.
  It supports the ES2023 specification including modules, asynchronous
  generators, proxies, BigInt, and BigFloat.

ORIGIN

  https://bellard.org/quickjs/
  https://github.com/bellard/quickjs

  Version: 2024-01-13 release

LICENSE

  MIT License - See LICENSE file for details
  Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Fabrice Bellard
  Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Charlie Gordon

LOCAL CHANGES

  - Imported for Cosmopolitan Libc build system
  - Uses Cosmopolitan's libc instead of system libc
  - Configured with CONFIG_BIGNUM for BigFloat/BigDecimal support

BUILDING

  make -j1 o//third_party/quickjs/qjs

USAGE

  o//third_party/quickjs/qjs script.js

  Or interactively:
  
  o//third_party/quickjs/qjs
  
  qjs > console.log("Hello from QuickJS!");
  Hello from QuickJS!

FILES

  quickjs.c, quickjs.h       - Core JavaScript engine
  quickjs-libc.c             - System bindings (stdio, sockets, etc.)
  libregexp.c                - Regular expression engine
  libunicode.c               - Unicode support
  libbf.c                    - BigFloat/BigDecimal arithmetic
  cutils.c                   - Utility functions
  qjs.c                      - Standalone interpreter
